{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the congruence \\(2n \\equiv 15 \\pmod{47}\\), we need to find the multiplicative inverse of 2 modulo 47. This means we need to find an integer \\(x\\) such that \\(2x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{47}\\).\n\nWe can use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find this inverse. We start by applying the Euclidean Algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of 2 and 47:\n\n\\[\n47 = 2 \\cdot 23 + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n2 = 1 \\cdot 2 + 0\n\\]\n\nThe gcd is 1, and we can backtrack to express 1 as a combination of 2 and 47:\n\n\\[\n1 = 47 - 2 \\cdot 23\n\\]\n\nThis tells us that \\( -23 \\) is a solution to \\(2x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{47}\\). Since we want a positive residue, we convert \\(-23\\) to a positive equivalent by adding 47:\n\n","prefix_end":683,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,30169,84,763,17767,17,77,1124,57317,220,16,20,1124,79,2593,90,19,22,11035,701,582,1184,311,1477,279,12557,65266,27949,315,220,17,59864,220,19,22,13,1096,3363,582,1184,311,1477,458,7546,17767,87,57758,1741,429,17767,17,87,1124,57317,220,16,1124,79,2593,90,19,22,11035,3593,1654,646,990,279,40565,21963,50078,40325,311,1477,419,27949,13,1205,1191,553,18950,279,21963,50078,40325,311,1477,279,12196,4185,49109,320,91289,8,315,220,17,323,220,19,22,1447,59,9640,19,22,284,220,17,1124,50853,220,17,18,488,220,16,198,59,921,59,9640,17,284,220,16,1124,50853,220,17,488,220,15,198,59,2533,785,44858,374,220,16,11,323,582,646,98921,311,3158,220,16,438,264,10601,315,220,17,323,220,19,22,1447,59,9640,16,284,220,19,22,481,220,17,1124,50853,220,17,18,198,59,2533,1986,10742,601,429,17767,481,17,18,1124,8,374,264,6291,311,17767,17,87,1124,57317,220,16,1124,79,2593,90,19,22,11035,568,8704,582,1366,264,6785,48132,11,582,5508,1124,4080,17,18,57758,311,264,6785,13578,553,7842,220,19,22,1447,59,9640,12,17,18,488,220,19,22,284,220,17,19,198,59,2533,4416,11,27